        {
            "@id": "/recipe/galbi-jjim/comment-page-4#sso/comment/31737",
            "@context": "https://schema.org",
            "@type": "Comment",
            "url": "https://www.maangchi.com/recipe/galbi-jjim/comment-page-4#comment-31737",
            "name": "Comment by mokpochica on January 3, 2012",
            "description": "I made this today for my family. My husband and one of my daughters went crazy for it. (My other&hellip;",
            "text": "I made this today for my family. My husband and one of my daughters went crazy for it. (My other 2 are sick and so aren&#039;t eating much right now.) This is definitely one to make again!",
            "dateCreated": "2012-01-03T02:35:20-05:00",
            "author": {
                "@context": "https://schema.org",
                "@type": "Person",
                "url": "http://ourthreelittleones.shutterfly.com/",
                "name": "mokpochica"
            }
        },
        {
            "@id": "/recipe/galbi-jjim/comment-page-4#sso/comment/30229",
            "@context": "https://schema.org",
            "@type": "Comment",
            "url": "https://www.maangchi.com/recipe/galbi-jjim/comment-page-4#comment-30229",
            "name": "Comment by pantaloons on November 22, 2011",
            "description": "Hi maangchi! I love this dish and I would love to make it. But my diet requires that I do&hellip;",
            "text": "Hi maangchi! I love this dish and I would love to make it. But my diet requires that I do not eat any processed sugars and also no corn starch. I can use natural sweetners like honey or agave. What would you recommend? I was thinking I could use honey instead of brow sugar and just skip the cornstarch. Thanks :)",
            "dateCreated": "2011-11-22T06:27:03-05:00",
            "author": {
                "@context": "https://schema.org",
                "@type": "Person",
                "name": "pantaloons"
            }
        },
        {
            "@id": "/recipe/galbi-jjim/comment-page-4#sso/comment/28222",
            "@context": "https://schema.org",
            "@type": "Comment",
            "url": "https://www.maangchi.com/recipe/galbi-jjim/comment-page-4#comment-28222",
            "name": "Comment by jinpong on October 19, 2011",
            "description": "I made this today but used slow cooker. I followed till 6 then popped all in slow cooker for 6&hellip;",
            "text": "I made this today but used slow cooker. I followed till 6 then popped all in slow cooker for 6 hrs. I also added the mulyot. It turned out good n soft but was bit watery. I did not add the sesame oil. What would you suggest? Less water and more soy sauce?",
            "dateCreated": "2011-10-19T03:13:52-04:00",
            "author": {
                "@context": "https://schema.org",
                "@type": "Person",
                "name": "jinpong"
            },
            "comment": [
                {
                    "@id": "/recipe/galbi-jjim/comment-page-4#sso/comment/31783"
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "@id": "/recipe/galbi-jjim/comment-page-4#sso/comment/31783",
            "@context": "https://schema.org",
            "@type": "Comment",
            "url": "https://www.maangchi.com/recipe/galbi-jjim/comment-page-4#comment-31783",
            "name": "Reply by koreanita on January 5, 2012",
            "description": "I like the slow cooker too when I&#039;m lazy and just want a hot meal when I get home from&hellip;",
            "text": "I like the slow cooker too when I&#039;m lazy and just want a hot meal when I get home from work. I just add enough water to cover the meat; then add more seasonings at the same time. The broth is really good! I just eat it with rice and add the broth in together like a stew and it&#039;s so good.",
            "dateCreated": "2012-01-05T16:34:26-05:00",
            "author": {
                "@context": "https://schema.org",
                "@type": "Person",
                "name": "koreanita"
            }
        },
        {
            "@id": "/recipe/galbi-jjim/comment-page-4#sso/comment/27193",
            "@context": "https://schema.org",
            "@type": "Comment",
            "url": "https://www.maangchi.com/recipe/galbi-jjim/comment-page-4#comment-27193",
            "name": "Comment by Tokki123 on July 26, 2011",
            "description": "Hi Maangchi - I love your website and youtube show. It&#039;s where I go when I feel homesick! I made&hellip;",
            "text": "Hi Maangchi - I love your website and youtube show. It&#039;s where I go when I feel homesick! I made this with short ribs, carrots, potatoes, shiitake mushrooms and chestnuts in a slow-cooker. The meat just melted off the bone - it was amazingly flavoursome! We didn&#039;t have any sauce left at the end either so clean up was no trouble ^^ Thanks so much!",
            "dateCreated": "2011-07-26T15:03:07-04:00",
            "author": {
                "@context": "https://schema.org",
                "@type": "Person",
                "name": "Tokki123"
            },
            "comment": [
                {
                    "@id": "/recipe/galbi-jjim/comment-page-4#sso/comment/27194"
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "@id": "/recipe/galbi-jjim/comment-page-4#sso/comment/27194",
            "@context": "https://schema.org",
            "@type": "Comment",
            "url": "https://www.maangchi.com/recipe/galbi-jjim/comment-page-4#comment-27194",
            "name": "Reply by catk on July 26, 2011",
            "description": "Hi Maangchi, My mom is here visiting and she is the kind of korean cook who also whips things out&hellip;",
            "text": "Hi Maangchi, My mom is here visiting and she is the kind of korean cook who also whips things out without measuring (or barely looking at what she&#039;s doing). I work all day but want to make this kalbi chim for my parents and want to throw it in the slow cooker. What instructions would you change to do it this way? I am really excited about your website and can&#039;t wait to make this dish! Thanks, Cat",
            "dateCreated": "2011-07-26T16:10:26-04:00",
            "author": {
                "@context": "https://schema.org",
                "@type": "Person",
                "name": "catk"
            },
            "comment": [
                {
                    "@id": "/recipe/galbi-jjim/comment-page-4#sso/comment/27229"
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "@id": "/recipe/galbi-jjim/comment-page-4#sso/comment/27229",
            "@context": "https://schema.org",
            "@type": "Comment",
            "url": "https://www.maangchi.com/recipe/galbi-jjim/comment-page-4#comment-27229",
            "name": "Reply by Tokki123 on July 29, 2011",
            "description": "Hi Cat - i followed Maangchi&#039;s recipe until step 6 (I boiled the ribs then place them in the slow&hellip;",
            "text": "Hi Cat - i followed Maangchi&#039;s recipe until step 6 (I boiled the ribs then place them in the slow cooker). I put all the remaining ingredients into the slow cooker at a &#039;low&#039; setting for 6 hours and literally just left it alone...but I suspect it may differ depending on your slow cooker? I hope it goes well for you! Tokki123",
            "dateCreated": "2011-07-29T08:53:17-04:00",
            "author": {
                "@context": "https://schema.org",
                "@type": "Person",
                "name": "Tokki123"
            },
            "comment": [
                {
                    "@id": "/recipe/galbi-jjim/comment-page-4#sso/comment/27233"
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "@id": "/recipe/galbi-jjim/comment-page-4#sso/comment/27233",
            "@context": "https://schema.org",
            "@type": "Comment",
            "url": "https://www.maangchi.com/recipe/galbi-jjim/comment-page-4#comment-27233",
            "name": "Reply by Maangchi on July 29, 2011",
            "description": "Hi Cat, nice meeting you through my website. Happy cooking! And Tokki123, thank you very much for sharing your cooking&hellip;",
            "text": "Hi Cat, nice meeting you through my website. Happy cooking! And Tokki123, thank you very much for sharing your cooking tip! : )",
            "dateCreated": "2011-07-29T12:50:17-04:00",
            "author": {
