" title="Korean cooking blog">Blog</a></li><li><a href="/letter" title="Maangchi's monthly letter">My Monthly Letter</a></li><li><a href="/contact" title="Contact Maangchi">Contact</a></li></ul></li><li class="no-subnav"> <a class="nav-top-link" href="/letter" title="Maangchi's monthly letter">Maangchi's Letter</a></li></ol></div></div><div id="shell" class="shell hfeed"><div id="content"><div id="content-body" class="content-body hentry"><h1 class="entry-title mega-heading">Braised beef short ribs</h1><h2 class="entry-title mega-heading-translation"><span class="romanized-name">Galbi-jjim</span> <span class="korean-name">갈비찜</span></h2><p class="author vcard postedby">By <a href="/about" rel="author"><span class="fn n nickname">Maangchi</span></a></p><p class="postdate updated">Updated on December 31st, 2022</p><div        class="rmp-widgets-container rmp-wp-plugin rmp-main-container js-rmp-widgets-container js-rmp-widgets-container--628 "        data-post-id="628"><div class="rmp-rating-widget js-rmp-rating-widget" role="group" aria-labelledby="rmp-title-628"><div class="rmp-rating-widget__icons"><ul class="rmp-rating-widget__icons-list js-rmp-rating-icons-list" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Rating from 1 to 5"><li                            class="rmp-rating-widget__icons-list__icon js-rmp-rating-item"                            data-descriptive-rating="Not at all useful"                            data-value="1"                            role="radio"                            aria-checked="false"                            aria-label="1 out of 5: Not at all useful"                            tabindex="0"                    > <i class="js-rmp-rating-icon rmp-icon rmp-icon--ratings rmp-icon--star rmp-icon--full-highlight" aria-hidden="true"></i></li><li                            class="rmp-rating-widget__icons-list__icon js-rmp-rating-item"                            data-descriptive-rating="Somewhat useful"                            data-value="2"                            role="radio"                            aria-checked="false"                            aria-label="2 out of 5: Somewhat useful"                            tabindex="-1"                    > <i class="js-rmp-rating-icon rmp-icon rmp-icon--ratings rmp-icon--star rmp-icon--full-highlight" aria-hidden="true"></i></li><li                            class="rmp-rating-widget__icons-list__icon js-rmp-rating-item"                            data-descriptive-rating="Good recipe"                            data-value="3"                            role="radio"                            aria-checked="false"                            aria-label="3 out of 5: Good recipe"                            tabindex="-1"                    > <i class="js-rmp-rating-icon rmp-icon rmp-icon--ratings rmp-icon--star rmp-icon--full-highlight" aria-hidden="true"></i></li><li                            class="rmp-rating-widget__icons-list__icon js-rmp-rating-item"                            data-descriptive-rating="Great recipe"                            data-value="4"                            role="radio"                            aria-checked="false"                            aria-label="4 out of 5: Great recipe"                            tabindex="-1"                    > <i class="js-rmp-rating-icon rmp-icon rmp-icon--ratings rmp-icon--star rmp-icon--full-highlight" aria-hidden="true"></i></li><li                            class="rmp-rating-widget__icons-list__icon js-rmp-rating-item"                            data-descriptive-rating="The besttt!!!"                            data-value="5"                            role="radio"                            aria-checked="false"                            aria-label="5 out of 5: The besttt!!!"                            tabindex="-1"                    > <i class="js-rmp-rating-icon rmp-icon rmp-icon--ratings rmp-icon--star rmp-icon--half-highlight js-rmp-replace-half-star" aria-hidden="true"></i></li></ul></div><p class="rmp-rating-widget__hover-text js-rmp-hover-text" aria-live="polite"></p> <button class="rmp-rating-widget__submit-btn rmp-btn js-submit-rating-btn"> Submit Rating </button><div aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"><p class="rmp-rating-widget__results js-rmp-results "> <span class="rmp-rating-widget__results__rating js-rmp-avg-rating">4.6</span>/5 from <span class="rmp-rating-widget__results__votes js-rmp-vote-count">629</span> votes</p><p class="rmp-rating-widget__not-rated js-rmp-not-rated rmp-rating-widget__not-rated--hidden"> Be the first to rate this.</p><p class="rmp-rating-widget__msg js-rmp-msg" role="status"></p></div></div></div> <style>lite-youtube {
			background-image: url('https://i.ytimg.com/vi/vtGzj6cUn7Q/default.jpg');
		}

		@media screen and (min-width: 320px) {
			lite-youtube {
				background-image: url('https://i.ytimg.com/vi/vtGzj6cUn7Q/hqdefault.jpg');
			}
		}

				@media screen and (min-width: 480px) {
			lite-youtube {
				background-image: url('https://i.ytimg.com/vi/vtGzj6cUn7Q/sddefault.jpg');
			}
		}

				@media screen and (min-width: 640px) {
			lite-youtube {
				background-image: url('https://i.ytimg.com/vi/vtGzj6cUn7Q/maxresdefault.jpg');
			}
		}</style><div class="hero-video-container"> <lite-youtube videoid="vtGzj6cUn7Q" allowfullscreen> <button href="https://youtube.com/watch?v=vtGzj6cUn7Q" class="lty-playbtn" title="Play Video"> <span class="lyt-visually-hidden">Play Galbi-jjim (Braised beef short ribs) 갈비찜 video</span> </button> </lite-youtube></div><div id="content-header" class="content-header"></div><div id="flex" class="flex"><div id="main" class="single-post"><div id="post-628" class="entry publish author-maangchi category-recipe"><div class="entry module"><p>Galbi-jjim (braised beef short ribs) is one of the most popular Korean dishes. It&#8217;s made with beef short ribs and is often prepared for special occasions.</p><p>Traditionally it&#8217;s a dish for special occasions such as Korean festival days like <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chuseok">Chuseok</a>, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Korean_New_Year">New Year&#8217;s Day (Seollal)</a>, or family&#8217;s birthdays, but you can make it for any occasion or as a weekend dish. It&#8217;s kind of a challenging recipe but the result is amazing: the meat is almost falling off the rib bones and is tender, sweet, savory, and irresistible.</p><p>This is a recipe from my <a href="https://www.maangchi.com/big/">new cookbook, Maangchi&#8217;s Big Book of Korean Cooking</a>, and it&#8217;s the first recipe I am posting in 2020, a remake of a recipe and video from 2008! This one is even more traditional than the one I posted 12 years ago, and includes ginkgo nuts, pine nuts, chestnuts and jujubes.</p><p>Choose good quality <a href="https://www.maangchi.com/ingredient/beef-short-ribs">short ribs</a> for this recipe, with lots of meat attached to the ribs. Remove the blood, excess fat, and impurities by soaking and blanching the ribs. If you skip this process, the final dish may smell off. Peak season for chestnuts is late fall, so if you use fresh chestnuts, that&#8217;s the best time. Fresh frozen skinned chestnuts are available all year round though, and available in the frozen section of Korean grocery stores. They also sell frozen ginkgo nuts, if you can&#8217;t find fresh ones.</p><p>I hope you enjoy this recipe, and make it for your friends and family! If any special guests coming over this will be a colorful center piece on the table. It&#8217;s January 5, 2020! I hope you are having a happy new year so far, and a prosperous and healthy new decade, too!</p><div class="recipe-card"><p><button class="print-recipe" onclick="window.print();return false;"><noscript><img decoding="async" src="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/themes/maangchi4/img/icons/print.svg" loading="lazy" width="20" height="20"></noscript><img src='data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22%20viewBox=%220%200%2020%2020%22%3E%3C/svg%3E' class="lazyload" decoding="async" data-src="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/themes/maangchi4/img/icons/print.svg" loading="lazy" width="20" height="20">Print recipe</button></p><div class="recipe-card-ingredients"><h2>Ingredients</h2><p>Serves 4</p><h3>For the seasoning sauce and vegetables:</h3><ul><li>4 dried <a href="https://www.maangchi.com/ingredient/shiitake-mushrooms">shiitake mushrooms</a>, washed and soaked in 2½ cups cold water for 3 to 4 hours, until soft</li><li>⅓ cup soy sauce</li><li>½ cup <a href="https://www.maangchi.com/ingredient/cooking-wine">mirim (aka mirin)</a>, or water</li><li>¼ cup sugar (white or brown, or <a href="https://amzn.to/2MXG4gB">swerve</a>)</li><li>½ teaspoon ground black pepper</li><li>8 garlic cloves, minced</li><li>1 teaspoon minced peeled <a href="https://www.maangchi.com/ingredient/ginger">ginger</a></li><li>1 medium size <a href="https://www.maangchi.com/ingredient/korean-radish">Korean radish</a> (8 ounces to 12 ounces) or <a href="https://www.maangchi.com/ingredient/daikon-radish">daikon</a>, peeled</li><li>2 large, thick carrots, peeled</li></ul><h3>For the beef short ribs:</h3><ul><li>2 pounds <a href="https://www.maangchi.com/ingredient/beef-short-ribs">beef short ribs</a> (8 pieces), rinsed and soaked in cold water for 30 minutes to 1 hour, changing water a couple of times</li><li>12 peeled frozen chestnuts or fresh chestnuts (see how to skin fresh chestnuts below; frozen are sold pre-skinned)</li><li>2 tablespoons <a href="https://www.maangchi.com/ingredient/rice-syrup">rice syrup</a></li><li>8 large dried <a href="https://www.maangchi.com/ingredient/jujubes">jujubes</a>, pitted</li></ul><p><a href="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/jujube.jpg"><img fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" class="aligncenter size-large wp-image-84915" src="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/jujube-650x366.jpg" alt="" width="620" height="349" srcset="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/jujube-650x366.jpg 650w, https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/jujube-620x349.jpg 620w, https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/jujube-134x75.jpg 134w" sizes="(max-width: 620px) 100vw, 620px" /></a></p><h3>For garnish:</h3><ul><li>12 <a href="https://www.maangchi.com/ingredient/pine-nuts">pine nuts</a>, tips removed (optional)</li><li>12 frozen ginkgo nuts, shelled and cooked (optional); see how to shell and cook ginkgo nuts below</li></ul></div><div class="recipe-card-directions"><h2>Directions</h2><h3>How to skin fresh chestnuts:</h3><ol><li>Lay the chestnut on the flat side and slice off the flat end, then slice off the pointed end.<a href="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/chestnuts2.jpg"><noscript><img decoding="async" class="aligncenter size-large wp-image-84893" src="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/chestnuts2-650x366.jpg" alt="" width="620" height="349" srcset="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/chestnuts2-650x366.jpg 650w, https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/chestnuts2-620x349.jpg 620w, https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/chestnuts2-134x75.jpg 134w" sizes="(max-width: 620px) 100vw, 620px" /></noscript><img src='data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22%20viewBox=%220%200%20620%20349%22%3E%3C/svg%3E' decoding="async" class="lazyload aligncenter size-large wp-image-84893" data-src="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/chestnuts2-650x366.jpg" alt="" width="620" height="349" data-srcset="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/chestnuts2-650x366.jpg 650w, https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/chestnuts2-620x349.jpg 620w, https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/chestnuts2-134x75.jpg 134w" data-sizes="(max-width: 620px) 100vw, 620px" /></a></li><li>Using a paring knife, slice down both of the narrower sides, removing the dark skin inside the shell.<a href="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/chestnuts3.jpg"><noscript><img decoding="async" class="aligncenter size-large wp-image-84894" src="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/chestnuts3-650x366.jpg" alt="" width="620" height="349" srcset="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/chestnuts3-650x366.jpg 650w, https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/chestnuts3-620x349.jpg 620w, https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/chestnuts3-134x75.jpg 134w" sizes="(max-width: 620px) 100vw, 620px" /></noscript><img src='data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22%20viewBox=%220%200%20620%20349%22%3E%3C/svg%3E' decoding="async" class="lazyload aligncenter size-large wp-image-84894" data-src="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/chestnuts3-650x366.jpg" alt="" width="620" height="349" data-srcset="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/chestnuts3-650x366.jpg 650w, https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/chestnuts3-620x349.jpg 620w, https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/chestnuts3-134x75.jpg 134w" data-sizes="(max-width: 620px) 100vw, 620px" /></a></li><li>Peel off the remaining shell with your fingers. Trim away the dark skin on the outside of the chestnut so that it is a uniform creamy color. <a href="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/chestnuts4.jpg"><noscript><img decoding="async" class="aligncenter size-large wp-image-84895" src="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/chestnuts4-650x366.jpg" alt="" width="620" height="349" srcset="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/chestnuts4-650x366.jpg 650w, https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/chestnuts4-620x349.jpg 620w, https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/chestnuts4-134x75.jpg 134w" sizes="(max-width: 620px) 100vw, 620px" /></noscript><img src='data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22%20viewBox=%220%200%20620%20349%22%3E%3C/svg%3E' decoding="async" class="lazyload aligncenter size-large wp-image-84895" data-src="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/chestnuts4-650x366.jpg" alt="" width="620" height="349" data-srcset="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/chestnuts4-650x366.jpg 650w, https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/chestnuts4-620x349.jpg 620w, https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/chestnuts4-134x75.jpg 134w" data-sizes="(max-width: 620px) 100vw, 620px" /></a></li></ol><h3>How to cook ginkgo nuts:</h3><ol><li>Heat about 2 teaspoons vegetable oil in a skillet over medium-high heat and add some shelled ginkgo nuts.</li><li>Add some salt and stir-fry until the skins loosen and the color of the nuts changes to golden or bright green.<a href="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/gingko-nuts-1.jpg"><noscript><img decoding="async" class="aligncenter size-large wp-image-84898" src="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/gingko-nuts-1-650x366.jpg" alt="" width="620" height="349" srcset="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/gingko-nuts-1-650x366.jpg 650w, https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/gingko-nuts-1-620x349.jpg 620w, https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/gingko-nuts-1-134x75.jpg 134w" sizes="(max-width: 620px) 100vw, 620px" /></noscript><img src='data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22%20viewBox=%220%200%20620%20349%22%3E%3C/svg%3E' decoding="async" class="lazyload aligncenter size-large wp-image-84898" data-src="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/gingko-nuts-1-650x366.jpg" alt="" width="620" height="349" data-srcset="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/gingko-nuts-1-650x366.jpg 650w, https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/gingko-nuts-1-620x349.jpg 620w, https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/gingko-nuts-1-134x75.jpg 134w" data-sizes="(max-width: 620px) 100vw, 620px" /></a></li><li>Transfer to paper towels, fold the paper towels over the nuts, and gently massage the nuts to remove more skin.</li></ol><h3>Make the seasoning sauce and vegetables:</h3><ol><li>After soaking the mushrooms, place a strainer over a bowl and drain.</li><li>Measure out 2 cups of the soaking water. If it can&#8217;t make 2 cups, fill it with cold water. Transfer to a medium bowl; discard the remainder if you have.</li><li>Add the soy sauce, mirim, sugar (or swerve), ground black pepper, garlic, and ginger and mix well with a spoon. Set the seasoning sauce aside.<a href="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbijjim-seasoning-sauce-scaled.jpg"><noscript><img decoding="async" class="aligncenter size-large wp-image-84900" src="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbijjim-seasoning-sauce-650x365.jpg" alt="galbi jjim sauce" width="620" height="348" /></noscript><img src='data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22%20viewBox=%220%200%20620%20348%22%3E%3C/svg%3E' decoding="async" class="lazyload aligncenter size-large wp-image-84900" data-src="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbijjim-seasoning-sauce-650x365.jpg" alt="galbi jjim sauce" width="620" height="348" /></a></li><li>Remove the stem from each mushroom and reserve for future use, like stir-fried rice. Cut each mushroom cap into quarters and transfer to a plate.</li><li>Cut the radish into 1½-inch cubes and round the edges of each cube with a paring knife to make approximately 1-inch balls. Make 10 to 12 balls. Add to the plate with the mushrooms.<a href="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/radish-ball.jpg"><noscript><img decoding="async" class="aligncenter size-large wp-image-84912" src="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/radish-ball-650x366.jpg" alt="" width="620" height="349" srcset="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/radish-ball-650x366.jpg 650w, https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/radish-ball-620x349.jpg 620w, https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/radish-ball-134x75.jpg 134w" sizes="(max-width: 620px) 100vw, 620px" /></noscript><img src='data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22%20viewBox=%220%200%20620%20349%22%3E%3C/svg%3E' decoding="async" class="lazyload aligncenter size-large wp-image-84912" data-src="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/radish-ball-650x366.jpg" alt="" width="620" height="349" data-srcset="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/radish-ball-650x366.jpg 650w, https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/radish-ball-620x349.jpg 620w, https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/radish-ball-134x75.jpg 134w" data-sizes="(max-width: 620px) 100vw, 620px" /></a><a href="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbijjim-radish-ball.jpg"><noscript><img decoding="async" class="aligncenter size-large wp-image-84911" src="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbijjim-radish-ball-650x366.jpg" alt="radish balls" width="620" height="349" srcset="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbijjim-radish-ball-650x366.jpg 650w, https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbijjim-radish-ball-620x349.jpg 620w, https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbijjim-radish-ball-134x75.jpg 134w" sizes="(max-width: 620px) 100vw, 620px" /></noscript><img src='data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22%20viewBox=%220%200%20620%20349%22%3E%3C/svg%3E' decoding="async" class="lazyload aligncenter size-large wp-image-84911" data-src="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbijjim-radish-ball-650x366.jpg" alt="radish balls" width="620" height="349" data-srcset="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbijjim-radish-ball-650x366.jpg 650w, https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbijjim-radish-ball-620x349.jpg 620w, https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbijjim-radish-ball-134x75.jpg 134w" data-sizes="(max-width: 620px) 100vw, 620px" /></a></li><li>Cut the carrots into 1½-inch cubes and round the edges of each cube with a paring knife to make approximately 1-inch balls. Make 10 to 12 balls. Add to the mushrooms and radish balls. <a href="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/carrot-ball.jpg"><noscript><img decoding="async" class="aligncenter size-large wp-image-84913" src="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/carrot-ball-650x366.jpg" alt="" width="620" height="349" srcset="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/carrot-ball-650x366.jpg 650w, https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/carrot-ball-620x349.jpg 620w, https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/carrot-ball-134x75.jpg 134w" sizes="(max-width: 620px) 100vw, 620px" /></noscript><img src='data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22%20viewBox=%220%200%20620%20349%22%3E%3C/svg%3E' decoding="async" class="lazyload aligncenter size-large wp-image-84913" data-src="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/carrot-ball-650x366.jpg" alt="" width="620" height="349" data-srcset="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/carrot-ball-650x366.jpg 650w, https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/carrot-ball-620x349.jpg 620w, https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/carrot-ball-134x75.jpg 134w" data-sizes="(max-width: 620px) 100vw, 620px" /></a><a href="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbijjim-vegetables-scaled.jpg"><noscript><img decoding="async" class="aligncenter size-large wp-image-84901" src="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbijjim-vegetables-650x365.jpg" alt="galbijjim vegetables" width="620" height="348" /></noscript><img src='data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22%20viewBox=%220%200%20620%20348%22%3E%3C/svg%3E' decoding="async" class="lazyload aligncenter size-large wp-image-84901" data-src="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbijjim-vegetables-650x365.jpg" alt="galbijjim vegetables" width="620" height="348" /></a></li></ol><h3>Cook the beef short ribs:</h3><ol><li>Fill a large, heavy pot halfway with water and bring to a boil over medium-high heat. Drain the ribs, rinse again, and add to the boiling water.<a href="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbi-blanch.jpg"><noscript><img decoding="async" class="aligncenter size-large wp-image-84902" src="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbi-blanch-650x366.jpg" alt="" width="620" height="349" srcset="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbi-blanch-650x366.jpg 650w, https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbi-blanch-620x349.jpg 620w, https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbi-blanch-134x75.jpg 134w" sizes="(max-width: 620px) 100vw, 620px" /></noscript><img src='data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22%20viewBox=%220%200%20620%20349%22%3E%3C/svg%3E' decoding="async" class="lazyload aligncenter size-large wp-image-84902" data-src="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbi-blanch-650x366.jpg" alt="" width="620" height="349" data-srcset="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbi-blanch-650x366.jpg 650w, https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbi-blanch-620x349.jpg 620w, https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbi-blanch-134x75.jpg 134w" data-sizes="(max-width: 620px) 100vw, 620px" /></a></li><li>Blanch for 5 minutes, stirring a few times. Drain and rinse thoroughly with cold water. Wash the pot with soapy water nicely.<a href="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbi-wash.jpg"><noscript><img decoding="async" class="aligncenter size-large wp-image-84903" src="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbi-wash-650x366.jpg" alt="" width="620" height="349" srcset="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbi-wash-650x366.jpg 650w, https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbi-wash-620x349.jpg 620w, https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbi-wash-134x75.jpg 134w" sizes="(max-width: 620px) 100vw, 620px" /></noscript><img src='data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22%20viewBox=%220%200%20620%20349%22%3E%3C/svg%3E' decoding="async" class="lazyload aligncenter size-large wp-image-84903" data-src="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbi-wash-650x366.jpg" alt="" width="620" height="349" data-srcset="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbi-wash-650x366.jpg 650w, https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbi-wash-620x349.jpg 620w, https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbi-wash-134x75.jpg 134w" data-sizes="(max-width: 620px) 100vw, 620px" /></a></li><li>Put the ribs back to the pot and add the seasoning sauce. Cover and cook over medium-high heat for 20 minutes. <a href="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbijjim-add-sauce.jpg"><noscript><img decoding="async" class="aligncenter size-large wp-image-84914" src="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbijjim-add-sauce-650x366.jpg" alt="" width="620" height="349" srcset="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbijjim-add-sauce-650x366.jpg 650w, https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbijjim-add-sauce-620x349.jpg 620w, https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbijjim-add-sauce-134x75.jpg 134w" sizes="(max-width: 620px) 100vw, 620px" /></noscript><img src='data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22%20viewBox=%220%200%20620%20349%22%3E%3C/svg%3E' decoding="async" class="lazyload aligncenter size-large wp-image-84914" data-src="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbijjim-add-sauce-650x366.jpg" alt="" width="620" height="349" data-srcset="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbijjim-add-sauce-650x366.jpg 650w, https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbijjim-add-sauce-620x349.jpg 620w, https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbijjim-add-sauce-134x75.jpg 134w" data-sizes="(max-width: 620px) 100vw, 620px" /></a><a href="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbi-in-sauce.jpg"><noscript><img decoding="async" class="aligncenter size-large wp-image-84904" src="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbi-in-sauce-650x366.jpg" alt="" width="620" height="349" srcset="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbi-in-sauce-650x366.jpg 650w, https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbi-in-sauce-620x349.jpg 620w, https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbi-in-sauce-134x75.jpg 134w" sizes="(max-width: 620px) 100vw, 620px" /></noscript><img src='data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22%20viewBox=%220%200%20620%20349%22%3E%3C/svg%3E' decoding="async" class="lazyload aligncenter size-large wp-image-84904" data-src="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbi-in-sauce-650x366.jpg" alt="" width="620" height="349" data-srcset="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbi-in-sauce-650x366.jpg 650w, https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbi-in-sauce-620x349.jpg 620w, https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbi-in-sauce-134x75.jpg 134w" data-sizes="(max-width: 620px) 100vw, 620px" /></a></li><li>Stir in the mushrooms, chestnuts, radishes, and carrots. Cover, turn down the heat to low, and cook for 1 hour, stirring occasionally.</li><li>Stir in the jujubes and rice syrup.<a href="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbijjim-rice-syrup.jpg"><noscript><img decoding="async" class="aligncenter size-large wp-image-84905" src="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbijjim-rice-syrup-650x366.jpg" alt="galbi jjim (Korean braised beef short ribs)" width="620" height="349" srcset="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbijjim-rice-syrup-650x366.jpg 650w, https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbijjim-rice-syrup-620x349.jpg 620w, https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbijjim-rice-syrup-134x75.jpg 134w" sizes="(max-width: 620px) 100vw, 620px" /></noscript><img src='data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22%20viewBox=%220%200%20620%20349%22%3E%3C/svg%3E' decoding="async" class="lazyload aligncenter size-large wp-image-84905" data-src="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbijjim-rice-syrup-650x366.jpg" alt="galbi jjim (Korean braised beef short ribs)" width="620" height="349" data-srcset="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbijjim-rice-syrup-650x366.jpg 650w, https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbijjim-rice-syrup-620x349.jpg 620w, https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbijjim-rice-syrup-134x75.jpg 134w" data-sizes="(max-width: 620px) 100vw, 620px" /></a></li><li>Cover and simmer for another 10 minutes, or until the meat is just about falling off the bone. Thicker short ribs will take longer. To check, poke the meat with a wooden skewer. If the meat is tender enough to serve, the skewer should go through easily. If it does not, add some water (about 1 cup) and cook a little longer, anywhere from 15 to 30 minutes, depending on the thickness of the short ribs.</li><li>Increase the heat to high and spoon any remaining broth from the bottom of the pot over the meat and vegetables for a few minutes, until most of the sauce has reduced and the meat and vegetables are nicely glazed. <a href="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbijjim-glazing.jpg"><noscript><img decoding="async" class="aligncenter size-large wp-image-84906" src="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbijjim-glazing-650x366.jpg" alt="galbijjim (Korean braised beef short ribs) 갈비찜" width="620" height="349" srcset="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbijjim-glazing-650x366.jpg 650w, https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbijjim-glazing-620x349.jpg 620w, https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbijjim-glazing-134x75.jpg 134w" sizes="(max-width: 620px) 100vw, 620px" /></noscript><img src='data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22%20viewBox=%220%200%20620%20349%22%3E%3C/svg%3E' decoding="async" class="lazyload aligncenter size-large wp-image-84906" data-src="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbijjim-glazing-650x366.jpg" alt="galbijjim (Korean braised beef short ribs) 갈비찜" width="620" height="349" data-srcset="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbijjim-glazing-650x366.jpg 650w, https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbijjim-glazing-620x349.jpg 620w, https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbijjim-glazing-134x75.jpg 134w" data-sizes="(max-width: 620px) 100vw, 620px" /></a></li></ol><h3>Serve:</h3><ol><li>Transfer to a large platter, sprinkle with the pine nuts (if using) and ginkgo nuts (if using), and serve with rice and more side dishes.<a href="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbijjim-insta.jpg"><noscript><img decoding="async" class="aligncenter size-large wp-image-84907" src="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbijjim-insta-650x650.jpg" alt="galbijjim (Korean braised beef short ribs) 갈비찜" width="620" height="620" srcset="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbijjim-insta-650x650.jpg 650w, https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbijjim-insta-620x620.jpg 620w, https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbijjim-insta-150x150.jpg 150w, https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbijjim-insta-75x75.jpg 75w" sizes="(max-width: 620px) 100vw, 620px" /></noscript><img src='data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22%20viewBox=%220%200%20620%20620%22%3E%3C/svg%3E' decoding="async" class="lazyload aligncenter size-large wp-image-84907" data-src="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbijjim-insta-650x650.jpg" alt="galbijjim (Korean braised beef short ribs) 갈비찜" width="620" height="620" data-srcset="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbijjim-insta-650x650.jpg 650w, https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbijjim-insta-620x620.jpg 620w, https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbijjim-insta-150x150.jpg 150w, https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/galbijjim-insta-75x75.jpg 75w" data-sizes="(max-width: 620px) 100vw, 620px" /></a></li></ol></div></div> <button class="print-recipe" onclick="window.print();return false;"> <noscript><img src="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/themes/maangchi4/img/icons/print.svg" loading="lazy" width="20" height="20"></noscript><img src='data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22%20viewBox=%220%200%2020%2020%22%3E%3C/svg%3E' class="lazyload" data-src="https://www.maangchi.com/wp-content/themes/maangchi4/img/icons/print.svg" loading="lazy" width="20" height="20"> Print recipe</button></div><div class="entry-metadata single-entry-metadata module"><p class="entry-metadata--date"> Posted on <span class="updated">Wednesday, September 10th, 2008</span>.
 Last updated on December 31, 2022. <br> Recipe type: <span><a href="https://www.maangchi.com/recipes/beef" rel="tag">beef</a>, <a href="https://www.maangchi.com/recipes/main-dishes" rel="tag">main dish</a>, <a href="https://www.maangchi.com/recipes/non-spicy" rel="tag">non spicy</a>, <a href="https://www.maangchi.com/recipes/banchan" rel="tag">side dish</a></span> <br /> Tagged as <a href="https://www.maangchi.com/tag/braised-beef-short-ribs" rel="tag">braised beef short ribs</a>, <a href="https://www.maangchi.com/tag/%ea%b0%88%eb%b9%84%ec%b0%9c" rel="tag">갈비찜</a>, <a href="https://www.maangchi.com/tag/galbi-jjim" rel="tag">galbi-jjim</a>, <a href="https://www.maangchi.com/tag/galbijjim" rel="tag">galbijjim</a>, <a href="https://www.maangchi.com/tag/kalbi" rel="tag">kalbi</a>, <a href="https://www.maangchi.com/tag/korean-beef-ribs-recipe" rel="tag">Korean beef ribs recipe</a>, <a href="https://www.maangchi.com/tag/korean-braised-beef-short-ribs" rel="tag">Korean braised beef short ribs</a>, <a href="https://www.maangchi.com/tag/korean-food" rel="tag">korean food</a>, <a href="https://www.maangchi.com/tag/korean-recipes" rel="tag">Korean recipes</a>, <a href="https://www.maangchi.com/tag/sogalbijjim" rel="tag">sogalbijjim</a></p></div></div><div class="newsletter-module substack-embed newsletter-signup-embed module"><h3>Get my <a href="https://maangchi.substack.com">Substack</a></h3><p>It's all about Korean cooking and is available to everyone, 100% free and sent out on the first of the month at 3pm. I hope you enjoy it!</p> <iframe src="https://maangchi.substack.com/embed" width="100%" height="320" style="border:1px solid #EEE; background:white;" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe></div><div class="module affiliate-links-shell"><h3 class="module-heading">Buy this recipe's ingredients online</h3><p>I really like <a href="https://sayweee.sjv.io/xkdR7k">Weee!</a> they deliver quality packaged and fresh Korean ingredients to the continental USA. Cheaper and better than Amazon! <a href="https://sayweee.sjv.io/xkdR7k">Check them out</a>!</p><h4>Ingredients are also on Amazon:</h4><div class="affiliate-cards-flex-wrapper"><div class='amazon-product-card'><a href='https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0143AVM22?tag=cookkorefoodw-20&amp;linkCode=ogi&amp;th=1&amp;psc=1' target='_blank'><noscript><img src='https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31xjBWIHGzL._SL160_.jpg' alt='Chung Jung One Oligo Rice Syru...' loading='lazy'></noscript><img src='data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22%20viewBox=%220%200%20210%20140%22%3E%3C/svg%3E' class="lazyload" data-src='https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31xjBWIHGzL._SL160_.jpg' alt='Chung Jung One Oligo Rice Syru...' loading='lazy'></a><p class='amazon-product-card-title'><a href='https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0143AVM22?tag=cookkorefoodw-20&amp;linkCode=ogi&amp;th=1&amp;psc=1' target='_blank'>Chung Jung One Oligo Rice Syru...</a></p></div><div class='amazon-product-card'><a href='https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0FQ4Q842C?tag=cookkorefoodw-20&amp;linkCode=ogi&amp;th=1&amp;psc=1' target='_blank'><noscript><img src='https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41wu24gjZ-L._SL160_.jpg' alt='KFOOD Korean Food KANG BONG SE...' loading='lazy'></noscript><img src='data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22%20viewBox=%220%200%20210%20140%22%3E%3C/svg%3E' class="lazyload" data-src='https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41wu24gjZ-L._SL160_.jpg' alt='KFOOD Korean Food KANG BONG SE...' loading='lazy'></a><p class='amazon-product-card-title'><a href='https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0FQ4Q842C?tag=cookkorefoodw-20&amp;linkCode=ogi&amp;th=1&amp;psc=1' target='_blank'>KFOOD Korean Food KANG BONG SE...</a></p></div><div class='amazon-product-card'><a href='https://www.amazon.com/dp/B00558RHB2?tag=cookkorefoodw-20&amp;linkCode=ogi&amp;th=1&amp;psc=1' target='_blank'><noscript><img src='https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41nimVxUaqL._SL160_.jpg' alt='Kikkoman - Traditionally Brewe...' loading='lazy'></noscript><img src='data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22%20viewBox=%220%200%20210%20140%22%3E%3C/svg%3E' class="lazyload" data-src='https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41nimVxUaqL._SL160_.jpg' alt='Kikkoman - Traditionally Brewe...' loading='lazy'></a><p class='amazon-product-card-title'><a href='https://www.amazon.com/dp/B00558RHB2?tag=cookkorefoodw-20&amp;linkCode=ogi&amp;th=1&amp;psc=1' target='_blank'>Kikkoman - Traditionally Brewe...</a></p></div><div class='amazon-product-card'><a href='https://www.amazon.com/dp/B003XDIU30?tag=cookkorefoodw-20&amp;linkCode=ogi&amp;th=1&amp;psc=1' target='_blank'><noscript><img src='https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41W8op1-4bL._SL160_.jpg' alt='Kikkoman Japan Made Soy Sauce,...' loading='lazy'></noscript><img src='data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22%20viewBox=%220%200%20210%20140%22%3E%3C/svg%3E' class="lazyload" data-src='https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41W8op1-4bL._SL160_.jpg' alt='Kikkoman Japan Made Soy Sauce,...' loading='lazy'></a><p class='amazon-product-card-title'><a href='https://www.amazon.com/dp/B003XDIU30?tag=cookkorefoodw-20&amp;linkCode=ogi&amp;th=1&amp;psc=1' target='_blank'>Kikkoman Japan Made Soy Sauce,...</a></p></div><div class='amazon-product-card'><a href='https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0051ONTXU?tag=cookkorefoodw-20&amp;linkCode=ogi&amp;th=1&amp;psc=1' target='_blank'><noscript><img src='https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41ag2UuqxhL._SL160_.jpg' alt='Kikkoman Naturally Brewed Soy ...' loading='lazy'></noscript><img src='data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22%20viewBox=%220%200%20210%20140%22%3E%3C/svg%3E' class="lazyload" data-src='https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41ag2UuqxhL._SL160_.jpg' alt='Kikkoman Naturally Brewed Soy ...' loading='lazy'></a><p class='amazon-product-card-title'><a href='https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0051ONTXU?tag=cookkorefoodw-20&amp;linkCode=ogi&amp;th=1&amp;psc=1' target='_blank'>Kikkoman Naturally Brewed Soy ...</a></p></div></div></div><div id="comments" class="comments module"><h3 class="module-heading">221 Comments:</h3><ol class="commentlist" id="singlecomments"><li id="comment-55015" class="comment byuser comment-author-lindleylew even thread-even depth-1"><div class="comment-entry"><div class="comment-author"> <span class="fn"><a href="https://www.maangchi.com/author/lindleylew" title="lindleylew&#039;s profile page">lindleylew</a></span> <span class="joined">joined 2/25</span> <span class="comment-count"><span class="comment-count-low">1 comment</span></span></div><div class="comment-meta">Posted <a href="#comment-55015" title="Permalink to this comment">January 31st, 2025 at 8:39 pm</a> <span class="meta-sep">|</span> <span class="comment-reply-link"><a rel="nofollow" class="comment-reply-link" href="https://www.maangchi.com/recipe/galbi-jjim/comment-page-5?replytocom=55015#respond" data-commentid="55015" data-postid="628" data-belowelement="comment-55015" data-respondelement="respond" data-replyto="Reply to lindleylew" aria-label="Reply to lindleylew">Reply to this comment</a></span> or <a href="/join">create a profile</a>.</div><div class="comment-content"><p>I made this for the first time tonight! I wanted to make it for Lunar New Year, but had to find a store that had the short ribs first. The actual cooking took quite a bit longer than expected because of the thickness of my short ribs. I started to get flustered it wouldn&#8217;t turn out, but I took my time and everything was fine in the end. Tasted great! :) I love your recipes, Maangchi! I had to make a profile to leave comments because I&#8217;ve been making a lot lately. I made your kimchi a few days ago. Tastes great now, but can&#8217;t wait for it to ferment for a couple weeks!</p></div></div></li></li><li id="comment-54931" class="comment byuser comment-author-littlepotatonoms odd alt thread-odd thread-alt depth-1"><div class="comment-entry"><div class="comment-author"> <span class="fn"><a href="https://www.maangchi.com/author/littlepotatonoms" title="littlepotatonoms&#039;s profile page">LittlePotatoNoms</a></span> <span class="joined">joined 10/24</span> <span class="comment-count"><span class="comment-count-low">1 comment</span></span></div><div class="comment-meta">Posted <a href="#comment-54931" title="Permalink to this comment">October 21st, 2024 at 1:10 am</a> <span class="meta-sep">|</span> <span class="comment-reply-link"><a rel="nofollow" class="comment-reply-link" href="https://www.maangchi.com/recipe/galbi-jjim/comment-page-5?replytocom=54931#respond" data-commentid="54931" data-postid="628" data-belowelement="comment-54931" data-respondelement="respond" data-replyto="Reply to LittlePotatoNoms" aria-label="Reply to LittlePotatoNoms">Reply to this comment</a></span> or <a href="/join">create a profile</a>.</div><div class="comment-content"><p>Hi!</p><p>Is it possible to make soup out of this? If so, do I just add more water?</p><p>Thank you.</p></div></div></li><ol class="children"><li id="comment-54934" class="comment byuser comment-author-maangchi bypostauthor even depth-2"><div class="comment-entry"><div class="comment-author"> <span class="fn"><a href="https://www.maangchi.com/author/maangchi" title="maangchi&#039;s profile page">Maangchi</a></span> <span class="location">New York City</span> <span class="joined">joined 8/08</span> <span class="comment-count">&amp; has <span class="comment-count-high">593 comments</span></span></div><div class="comment-meta">Posted <a href="#comment-54934" title="Permalink to this comment">October 28th, 2024 at 7:17 am</a> <span class="meta-sep">|</span> <span class="comment-reply-link"><a rel="nofollow" class="comment-reply-link" href="https://www.maangchi.com/recipe/galbi-jjim/comment-page-5?replytocom=54934#respond" data-commentid="54934" data-postid="628" data-belowelement="comment-54934" data-respondelement="respond" data-replyto="Reply to Maangchi" aria-label="Reply to Maangchi">Reply to this comment</a></span> or <a href="/join">create a profile</a>.</div><div class="comment-content"><p>It may be nice to make a delicious galbi-jjim in a stew-like style with a bit more broth. Try adding more water and adjust the soy sauce or salt to your taste while cooking. Good luck!</p></div></div></li></li></ol></li><li id="comment-54583" class="comment byuser comment-author-williamsmom odd alt thread-even depth-1"><div class="comment-entry"><div class="comment-author"> <span class="fn"><a href="https://www.maangchi.com/author/williamsmom" title="williamsmom&#039;s profile page">WilliamsMom</a></span> <span class="joined">joined 9/23</span> <span class="comment-count"><span class="comment-count-low">1 comment</span></span></div><div class="comment-meta">Posted <a href="#comment-54583" title="Permalink to this comment">September 18th, 2023 at 7:16 pm</a> <span class="meta-sep">|</span> <span class="comment-reply-link"><a rel="nofollow" class="comment-reply-link" href="https://www.maangchi.com/recipe/galbi-jjim/comment-page-5?replytocom=54583#respond" data-commentid="54583" data-postid="628" data-belowelement="comment-54583" data-respondelement="respond" data-replyto="Reply to WilliamsMom" aria-label="Reply to WilliamsMom">Reply to this comment</a></span> or <a href="/join">create a profile</a>.</div><div class="comment-content"><p>Is there a way I can make this in a slow cooker? If there is, would you be so kind to share? Thanks so much!</p></div></div></li></li><li id="comment-52912" class="comment byuser comment-author-mrsmaranon even thread-odd thread-alt depth-1"><div class="comment-entry"><div class="comment-author"> <span class="fn"><a href="https://www.maangchi.com/author/mrsmaranon" title="mrsmaranon&#039;s profile page">mrsmaranon</a></span> <span class="location">Orlando, FL</span> <span class="joined">joined 12/21</span> <span class="comment-count">&amp; has <span class="comment-count-low">1 comment</span></span></div><div class="comment-meta">Posted <a href="#comment-52912" title="Permalink to this comment">November 30th, 2021 at 10:29 pm</a> <span class="meta-sep">|</span> <span class="comment-reply-link"><a rel="nofollow" class="comment-reply-link" href="https://www.maangchi.com/recipe/galbi-jjim/comment-page-5?replytocom=52912#respond" data-commentid="52912" data-postid="628" data-belowelement="comment-52912" data-respondelement="respond" data-replyto="Reply to mrsmaranon" aria-label="Reply to mrsmaranon">Reply to this comment</a></span> or <a href="/join">create a profile</a>.</div><div class="comment-content"><p>Do I have to use Dried Shiitake Mushroom? Can I use Fresh Shiitake Mushroom? If I buy the Shiitake Mushroom fresh, do I still have to soak it for 4 hours?</p></div></div></li><ol class="children"><li id="comment-52932" class="comment byuser comment-author-maangchi bypostauthor odd alt depth-2"><div class="comment-entry"><div class="comment-author"> <span class="fn"><a href="https://www.maangchi.com/author/maangchi" title="maangchi&#039;s profile page">Maangchi</a></span> <span class="location">New York City</span> <span class="joined">joined 8/08</span> <span class="comment-count">&amp; has <span class="comment-count-high">593 comments</span></span></div><div class="comment-meta">Posted <a href="#comment-52932" title="Permalink to this comment">December 10th, 2021 at 9:28 am</a> <span class="meta-sep">|</span> <span class="comment-reply-link"><a rel="nofollow" class="comment-reply-link" href="https://www.maangchi.com/recipe/galbi-jjim/comment-page-5?replytocom=52932#respond" data-commentid="52932" data-postid="628" data-belowelement="comment-52932" data-respondelement="respond" data-replyto="Reply to Maangchi" aria-label="Reply to Maangchi">Reply to this comment</a></span> or <a href="/join">create a profile</a>.</div><div class="comment-content"><p>No, you don&#8217;t need to soak fresh shiitake mushrooms.</p></div></div></li></li></ol></li><li id="comment-50703" class="comment byuser comment-author-reesieluvsfood even thread-even depth-1"><div class="comment-entry"><div class="comment-author"> <span class="fn"><a href="https://www.maangchi.com/author/reesieluvsfood" title="reesieluvsfood&#039;s profile page">ReesieLuvsFood</a></span> <span class="location">Walbridge Ohio USA</span> <span class="joined">joined 4/20</span> <span class="comment-count">&amp; has <span class="comment-count-low">1 comment</span></span></div><div class="comment-meta">Posted <a href="#comment-50703" title="Permalink to this comment">April 22nd, 2020 at 3:15 pm</a> <span class="meta-sep">|</span> <span class="comment-reply-link"><a rel="nofollow" class="comment-reply-link" href="https://www.maangchi.com/recipe/galbi-jjim/comment-page-5?replytocom=50703#respond" data-commentid="50703" data-postid="628" data-belowelement="comment-50703" data-respondelement="respond" data-replyto="Reply to ReesieLuvsFood" aria-label="Reply to ReesieLuvsFood">Reply to this comment</a></span> or <a href="/join">create a profile</a>.</div><div class="comment-content"><p>You are my favorite  Maangchi! ♡</p></div></div></li></li></ol><div class="comments-nav"> More comments to read! Jump to page: <a class="prev page-numbers" href="https://www.maangchi.com/recipe/galbi-jjim/comment-page-4#comments">< Previous </a> <a class="page-numbers" href="https://www.maangchi.com/recipe/galbi-jjim/comment-page-1#comments">1</a> <span class="page-numbers dots">&hellip;</span> <a class="page-numbers" href="https://www.maangchi.com/recipe/galbi-jjim/comment-page-3#comments">3</a> <a class="page-numbers" href="https://www.maangchi.com/recipe/galbi-jjim/comment-page-4#comments">4</a> <span aria-current="page" class="page-numbers current">5</span></div><div id="respond"><h3>Leave a Reply</h3><div id="cancel-comment-reply"> <small><a rel="nofollow" id="cancel-comment-reply-link" href="/recipe/galbi-jjim#respond" style="display:none;">Click here to cancel reply.</a></small></div><p>You must <a href="/join">create a profile</a> and be <a class="dynamicLoginLink" href="/wp-login.php">logged in</a> to post a comment.</p> <script>var MAANG = MAANG || {};
				MAANG.makeLoginLink = (function() { //rewrite login links to incl redirects
					var loginLink;
